    "DESCRIPTION": [
      "A subcircular enclosure (diam. c. 40m) defined by a low earthen bank. Visible on Google Earth (Imagery date: 19 Jan 2020). A large enclosure (CL034-254----) lies c. 150m to the E.\n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 12 July 2023",
      "At the N end of a low NE-SW ridge in pasture. A circular enclosure (diam. c. 35m) defined by a low earthen bank. Visible on Google Earth (Imagery date: 19 Jan 2020).\n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 12 July 2023",
      "On a NW-facing slope in an area now forested. A circular area (diam. c. 52m) comprising a raised platform defined by a scarp. Visible on Digital Globe (22011-2013) in pasture.\n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 28 March 2023",
      "On a SE-facing slope in pasture. A circular enclosure (diam. c. 40m) defined by a bank and fosse visible as a parch mark on Digital Globe (2011-2013).\n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 10 Mary 2021",
      "On an E-facing slope in an undulating field in pasture. An oval enclosure (c. 29m E-W; c. 19m N-S) defined by a low earthen bank. Visible on Google Earth (Imagery date: 10 Feb 2021). \n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 12 July 2023",
      "On top of a low NNE-SSW ridge in pasture. An oval enclosure (c. 40m NE-SW; c. 25m NW-SE) defined by a low earthen bank visible on Google Earth (Imagery dates: 12 May 2019 and 10 Feb 2021).\n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 12 July 2023",
      "On top of a small drumlin in pasture. A circular platform (diam. c. 45m) defined by a scarp. Visible on Google Earth (Imagery date: 19 Jan 2020). \n\nCompiled by: Mary Tunney\n\nDate of upload: 12 July 2023",
      "See attached document with details from Risteárd Ua Cróinín and Martin Breen, The Castles and Tower-houses of Co. Clare (unpublished report). Uploaded courtesy of R. Ua Cróinín and M. Breen.\n\nDate of upload: 9 December 2014"
    ],
